@bs-humany/modules-nerves

This package is code, and its code is Apache-2.0 (see the root LICENSE). Its policies/ directory is
not code: the trained policies there are in the Data tier of ADR-009, by the owner's decision of
2026-09-27, and are distributed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
The licence text is the one in packages/skeleton/LICENSE and packages/muscle-data/LICENSE. That
holds for every checkpoint in policies/, the ones there today and any that replace them.

Each is a network's weights, found by searching against this project's simulated body: the
skeleton of @bs-humany/skeleton, the muscles of @bs-humany/muscle-data and the fibre lengths, ranges
and attachments measured on the bone meshes of @bs-humany/assets-anatomical. Every file names the
senses and muscles of that body, and what its weights are worth is what they do to it. So they are
treated as derivatives of the data they were trained on, and they carry its licence and its
attribution:

  "BodyParts3D - The Database Center for Life Science - CC-BY-SA 2.1 Japan"
  "Z-Anatomy - The libre 3D atlas of anatomy - CC-BY-SA 4.0"

Z-Anatomy authors: Kousaku Okubo (original BodyParts3D model), Gauthier Kervyn (design, 3D,
anatomy), Marcin Zielinski (Blender add-on), Lluis Vinent (Unity development).
Source: https://github.com/LluisV/Z-Anatomy (Resources/Models/FBX/SkeletalSystem100.fbx) and
https://github.com/Z-Anatomy/Models-of-human-anatomy.

The code that loads, runs and trains them -- src/ here and tools/train -- is not a derivative of
the weights and stays Apache-2.0, as the code that loads the skeleton does. See ADR-009, the tier
table in CONTRIBUTING.md and the root NOTICE.
